{"v": 5, "date": "2026-11-19", "title": "Snow on the peaks Sunday 22 November, and winter shows up around Tuesday 15 December", "brief": ["❄️ Sunday 22 November: snow on the peaks from about 2200 m up, up to about 32 cm on Monte Cusna (2121 m).", "👀 Thursday 26 November is the day to mark next week: snow shows up in about one scenario in five.", "🥶 Around Tuesday 15 December the cold gains strength: for now it shows up in about one scenario in five.", "🌍 The big picture, from the Arctic to the stratosphere, points the same way."], "sections": [{"h": "The next few days", "p": ["Saturday: good weather pretty much everywhere, pick the handiest spot. The most interesting moment is Sunday 22 November: snow falls on the peaks from about 2200 m up, and about 32 cm could pile up on Monte Cusna (2121 m). It's a quick pass: the next updates will confirm it."]}, {"h": "From Tue 24 to Sat 28", "p": ["A mix of storms with snow only on the highest peaks and dry days with normal temperatures, with temperatures at altitude around +4 °C. Snow, at least on the peaks, shows up in about one scenario in five: the most promising day is Thursday 26 November."]}, {"h": "From Sun 29 to Thu 3", "p": ["A mix of dry, mild days and storms with snow only on the highest peaks, with temperatures at altitude around +5 °C. Snow, at least on the peaks, shows up in about one scenario in ten: the most promising day is Sunday 29 November."]}, {"h": "From Fri 4 to Fri 18", "p": ["A mix of dry, mild days and storms with snow only on the highest peaks, with temperatures at altitude around +4 °C. Snow, at least on the peaks, shows up in about one scenario in ten: the most promising day is Thursday 17 December. Keep an eye on the cold: in about one scenario in five the air at 1500 m drops below −2 °C, mainly around Tuesday 15 December."]}, {"h": "Why people are talking about cold", "p": ["Something rare happened in mid-November: around Tuesday 10 November the stratospheric winds over the Pole reversed. It usually happens in the depths of winter, and never this early. When it does, cold air has more chances to head down towards Europe in the following weeks. The Arctic Oscillation is also dropping, pointing the same way. The Atlantic, on the other hand, gives no clear signal yet. In plain words: cold is more likely than usual between Tuesday 24 November and Tuesday 8 December, but it's not certain, and we don't yet know whether it will reach us or stop further east. For now the models see it in about one scenario in five: if that number rises in the coming days, here it comes."]}], "ground": "The official stations don't measure any snow on the ground yet: the season has yet to begin.", "lead": ["Sunday 22 November: snow on the peaks from about 2200 m up, up to about 32 cm on Monte Cusna (2121 m). Thursday 26 November is the day to mark next week: snow shows up in about one scenario in five."], "chart": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 900 250\" class=\"syn-chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Temperature trend at 1,500 m\"><rect x=\"30\" y=\"101.7\" width=\"840\" height=\"60.3\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" opacity=\".7\"/><line x1=\"30\" x2=\"870\" y1=\"101.7\" y2=\"101.7\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"115.7\" class=\"lbl snow\">❄ snow down to resorts below 0 °C</text><line x1=\"30\" x2=\"870\" y1=\"101.7\" y2=\"101.7\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/><polygon points=\"30.0,25.4 59.0,35.7 87.9,43.9 116.9,50.2 145.9,44.5 174.8,58.3 203.8,43.0 232.8,31.5 261.7,30.7 290.7,31.0 319.7,31.4 348.6,20.6 377.6,26.3 406.6,21.0 435.5,30.3 464.5,33.7 493.4,28.1 522.4,31.8 551.4,31.8 580.3,40.6 609.3,38.9 638.3,38.0 667.2,45.6 696.2,49.8 725.2,27.2 754.1,36.3 783.1,32.5 812.1,37.9 841.0,45.9 870.0,28.5 870.0,109.8 841.0,120.1 812.1,122.3 783.1,130.4 754.1,122.8 725.2,115.5 696.2,105.2 667.2,112.4 638.3,117.9 609.3,132.2 580.3,125.8 551.4,130.1 522.4,134.6 493.4,124.3 464.5,122.4 435.5,100.4 406.6,107.9 377.6,96.5 348.6,103.3 319.7,124.9 290.7,108.2 261.7,105.7 232.8